{
  "command": "entire doctor",
  "short": "Diagnose and fix session issues",
  "long": "Scan for session issues and offer to fix them.\n\nChecks performed:\n  1. Disconnected metadata branches: detects when local and remote\n     entire/checkpoints/v1 branches share no common ancestor (caused by a\n     previous bug). Fixes by cherry-picking local checkpoints onto remote tip.\n\n  2. Operational logs: warn when .entire/logs cannot be written. Every other\n     diagnostic is delivered by writing there, and that write is silent about\n     its own failure, so an unwritable log directory looks exactly like a repo\n     where nothing ran.\n\n  When Codex hooks are installed:\n  3. Codex hook trust: warn when hooks declared in .codex/hooks.json\n     lack a trusted_hash entry in the user's Codex config (i.e. /hooks\n     review hasn't run yet on this machine, or a newer entire release\n     added a hook the user hasn't approved yet).\n\n  For each installed agent that reports hook-config drift:\n  4. Hook config: warn when the installed hooks no longer match what this\n     CLI writes (e.g. an older release wrote Claude Code tool matchers that\n     no longer fire, or a committed Pi/OpenCode extension has gone stale).\n     Fix by re-running 'entire enable --force'.\n\n  5. Stuck sessions: sessions stuck in ACTIVE or ENDED phase that need cleanup.\n\nA session is considered stuck if:\n  - It is in ACTIVE phase with no interaction for over 1 hour\n  - It is in ENDED phase with uncondensed checkpoint data on a shadow branch\n\nFor each stuck session, you can choose to:\n  - Condense: Save session data to permanent storage\n  - Discard: Remove the session state and shadow branch data\n  - Skip: Leave the session as-is\n\nUse --force to condense all fixable sessions without prompting.  Sessions that can't\nbe condensed will be discarded.\n\nWithout a terminal to prompt on (agents, CI), doctor reports each issue and\npoints at --force instead of prompting.",
  "repo": "gh/MuskanPaliwal/cli",
  "flags": [
    {
      "name": "force",
      "shorthand": "f",
      "type": "bool",
      "default": "false",
      "usage": "Auto-fix all issues without prompting"
    },
    {
      "name": "context",
      "type": "string",
      "usage": "Act as this saved login `name` for this command only, instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)"
    }
  ],
  "subcommands": [
    {
      "name": "bundle",
      "short": "Produce a diagnostic bundle (zip) for bug reports — secrets are redacted by default"
    },
    {
      "name": "logs",
      "short": "Show recent operational logs"
    },
    {
      "name": "migrate-checkpoints",
      "short": "Convert git-branch checkpoints into per-checkpoint git refs (git-refs store)"
    },
    {
      "name": "trace",
      "short": "Show hook performance traces"
    }
  ]
}

